{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'dir=\"$PWD\"; while [ \"$dir\" != / ]; do if [ -f \"$dir/AGENTS.md\" ]; then cat \"$dir/AGENTS.md\"; fi; dir=$(dirname \"$dir\"); done; node --version; cat src/parse.ts README.md'","aggregated_output":"v24.14.1\nimport { DurationError } from \"./errors.ts\";\nimport { SECONDS_PER_UNIT } from \"./units.ts\";\n\nconst PART = /(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)([a-z]+)/g;\n\n/** Seconds in a duration such as `1h30m` or `1.5h` (not rounded). */\nexport function parseDuration(text: string): number {\n  const value = text.trim().toLowerCase();\n  if (value === \"\") {\n    throw new DurationError(\"empty duration\");\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  let consumed = 0;\n  for (const match of value.matchAll(PART)) {\n    const [whole, amount, unit] = match;\n    const size = SECONDS_PER_UNIT.get(unit);\n    if (size === undefined) {\n      throw new DurationError(`unknown unit \"${unit}\" in \"${text}\"`);\n    }\n    if (match.index !== consumed) {\n      break;\n    }\n    total += Number(amount) * size;\n    consumed += whole.length;\n  }\n  if (consumed !== value.length) {\n    throw new DurationError(`cannot read \"${text}\"`);\n  }\n  return total;\n}\n# durations\n\nAdd up and summarise durations written like `1h30m`, `45s` or `2d4h`.\n\n```bash\nnode src/cli.ts total 1h30m 45m        # 2h15m\nnode src/cli.ts stats --file laps.txt  # count, total, fastest, slowest, average\n```\n\nUnits: `d` (days), `h`, `m`, `s`. Amounts may have decimals (`1.5h`). Results are rounded to the\nnearest second and printed largest unit first, leaving out zero parts (`0s` for nothing).\n\nErrors print `error: <message>` and exit with status 2.\n\nRun the tests with `npm test` (Node 24 runs the TypeScript files directly).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
